# Task2 harness work and memory ledger

No production file or candidate algorithm changes. The cold cloned tests retain every accepted exact numerical predicate and construction; instrumentation adds only diagnostic work. The original candidate ledger remains authoritative for hot candidate cost and memory. Changes here occur during test setup, each test assertion, each recorded API attempt, each observed elimination event and unit serialization, never a timed production path.

## Source-bound direct call schedule

Numerical streams, identical both modes: 26 cells, 52 ordinary constructors (26 reference factory calls and26 candidate wrapper factory calls), 512 replacements,1536 FTRAN,512 BTRAN. Each cell with u updates has1reference+1candidate constructor, u reference+u candidate replacements,6u FTRAN and2u BTRAN. There are256 cold ephemeral reference wrappers in addition to26 candidate wrappers; this does not add factorizations. No explicit refactor/copy occurs in streams. These are pre-entry API counts, not complete native/internal work accounting.

Lifecycle two backend cases:2candidate constructors,4 successful updates plus2busy+2bad-tolerance update attempts;6successful refactors plus2busy refactor attempts;4successful factor copies plus2busy copy attempts;10successful FTRAN plus2busy FTRAN attempts;2busy BTRAN attempts. The reentrant microcase adds1 FTRAN attempt rejected before inner solve. Micro suite:12 identity constructors and12 elimination attempts (8ordinary namespace,4fault namespace). It adds no intended successful solve. Exact fixture/carrier/matrix construction, original factory factorization/import and internal backend work are additional, not zero. The Python auditor binds all direct attempt counts including expected throws.

Task1 carriers perform no basis factorization/solve; exact9x9 history actions are additional arithmetic. The fixed structural tests create dense matrices up to96 (the4096/4097 cases check dimensions/charge only). They contain one cheap-reject allocation check, three repeated panel commits, exact dictionary oracles and fault/rejection controls. `panel_counts()` freezes each site's fixed loop multiplier.

## Diagnostic overhead and bounds

160 assertion sites are the maximum universe; active unit holds bounded dictionaries of used sites, API names and callback event names, not a per-pivot growing record. Each assertion increments one dictionary entry and temporarily binds its site; every API wrapper increments before dispatch, including rejected attempts; every traced pivot increments a scalar counter before rollback. Test aggregates form a fixed tree (four Task1 children, one lifecycle child, no stream child). Failure details are capped at200 records per unit; overflow rejects auditing. Expressions are evaluated once, and no counter work is placed inside the `@allocated` expression.

The harness retains one unit's recorder data. It serializes one unit file at a time and does not accumulate prior tests or numerical matrices in the driver. The existing `run_stream` returns <=32 fixed-field observations; serialization copies their five fields. These small diagnostic allocations and IO are included in process duration, not allocation/performance measurements. 28unit files+one raw file, guard pins/current/process/resources/log plus launcher/run-control files. Test macros and TOML formatting add allocation/storage; no native-free or fixed-byte claim.

Existing tests dominate cold cost: Trace keeps H/shadow/T and optional rollback copies, base snapshots, pivot/event vectors bounded by n and update, independent rational history and matrix products; these were already accepted in Task2. Exact relation checks are O(n^3) per finish, with arbitrary-precision numerator/denominator growth not bounded by Float64 payload size. Original-B residuals repeatedly rationalize B and vectors. Native factorization/import/solve/JIT/GC/initialization are additional. Guarded availableRAM/swap/VM limits bound execution safety; they do not prove the roster fits300s or a complete backend allocation budget.

For numerical streams raw pivot attempts (scalar+panel+pure rows) are capped at2u*(n-1+8): each side at most n-1 accepted steps, subject at most8 repeated private steps on its one rejection/update. Both stream sides must finish each update. Rejection/commit/begin bookkeeping and minimum-panel observations are independently reconciled with fixed u. Lifecycle traced microcases retain their own original assertions; event counts are recorded without inferring a hot-path speedup.

Candidate workspace payload remains72n+16ceil(9n/64)+4352:11488 at96,23360 at256,308480 at4096, <=1MiB. Whole changed-column arrays, old/new coexistence, incidence capacity, original factors, cache/history and diagnostic exact matrices are additional. No extra candidate tile, production vector scan, factor solve or invariant recheck is introduced by this harness. Whether the candidate saves time/allocations remains untested and belongs to a later Task3.
